    <h3>Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Always take a "clean baseline" snapshot</strong> immediately after installing each VM. This is your nuclear option — restore if everything goes wrong.</li>
      <li><strong>Take snapshots before and after</strong> each lab session so you have both a known-good state and a record of what you accomplished.</li>
      <li><strong>Name snapshots clearly</strong> with dates and session context: <code>2025-01-15_before-vsftpd-exploit</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete old snapshots</strong> periodically — each snapshot consumes additional disk space.</li>
      <li><strong>Do not rely on snapshots as backup</strong> — they live on the same physical disk. Back up VM folders to an external drive separately.</li>
    </ul>
