        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Kali Linux VM created — 2 adapters: NAT + Host-Only</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Kali installed, Guest Additions installed, tools verified</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Kali baseline snapshot taken: <code>Kali-Clean-Baseline</code></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Metasploitable 2 VM created — 1 adapter: Host-Only only</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Metasploitable baseline snapshot taken</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Connectivity verified: <code>ping 192.168.56.20</code> from Kali succeeds</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Nmap scan verified: <code>nmap -sV 192.168.56.20</code> shows open ports</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Network isolation verified: target VM has NO internet access</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:8px">☐ Lab policy established: snapshots before every session</li>
